From b8f78c43ed821b065350abacf8d38c84667c1de0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri Geelen <dimitri@geelenandcompany.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:17:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] fabric traverse: plain-string depends_on entries no
 longer crash impact into an empty chain (from 832 T-908/T-1025)

Some cards record depends_on entries as plain strings ("tools/x.py") instead of {type,target}
dicts. dep.get('type') raised on them, the traversal's stderr went to /dev/null, and
`fw fabric impact` printed an EMPTY chain: "nothing depends on this file", the answer
CLAUDE.md asks for before modifying a file. A crash rendered as reassurance.
Now: isinstance(dep, dict) guards at each read; the stderr masks are gone; a traversal that
fails prints IMPACT NOT COMPUTED and exits non-zero.
Probe: tests/unit/test_t1021_fabric_impact.sh (hermetic scratch fabric). Before: 0/2. After: 2/2.
Unchanged before and after: tests/unit/fabric.bats (10 ok), tests/integration/fw_fabric.bats (10 ok).
---
